  "answer": "Here is the recipe for Sesame and Soy Roasted Aubergine:\n\nIngredients:\n- Aubergine: 800 g (halved lengthways, scored)\n- Light soy sauce: 60 g\n- Mirin: 45 g\n- Toasted sesame oil: 20 g\n- Caster sugar: 15 g\n- Rice vinegar: 15 g\n- Ginger, grated: 15 g\n- Toasted sesame seeds: 12 g (to finish)\n- Spring onion: 40 g (sliced on the bias)\n\nMethod:\n1. Score the cut faces of the aubergine in a close diamond pattern, going most of the way through the flesh but not the skin. Salt them lightly and leave cut side down on paper for fifteen minutes to draw off water.\n2. Whisk the soy, mirin, sugar, vinegar and ginger into a glaze. Brush a third of it into the scored flesh and roast cut side up at 200 C for 25 minutes.\n3. Brush again and roast for a further ten minutes, until the flesh is completely collapsed and the surface lacquered. Finish with the sesame oil off the heat — heating it destroys the aroma — then the sesame seeds and spring onion.\n\nAllergens:\nContains soy (soy sauce), sesame and wheat (most soy sauce contains wheat; use tamari for a gluten free version).",
